# No em dashes

Never use the em dash character (Unicode U+2014) in documentation, skills, rules, or generated markdown.

## Prefer instead

| Intent | Use |
| --- | --- |
| Pause / aside | comma, period, or parentheses |
| Label then detail | colon (`:`) |
| Compound or empty table cell | plain hyphen (`-`) |
| Numeric / date ranges | plain hyphen (`1-2`, `2025-2026`) or `to` |

## Examples

- Bad: `You're here` + em dash + `welcome.`
- Good: `You're here. Welcome.` or `You're here: welcome.`

- Bad: heading with em dash between title and subtitle
- Good: `Tokenomics: EASY on XPR`

- Bad: empty table cell as an em dash
- Good: `-`

Also avoid en dashes (Unicode U+2013) in prose; use a hyphen or `to` for ranges.
